# Asset library — API keys
#
# Each variable below powers an asset panel that fetches from a third-party
# API. Without the key, the panel renders a "not configured" empty state with
# a setup link — nothing blocks app boot. Copy this file to `.env.local` and
# fill the keys you want to enable, then restart the dev server.
#
# Pre-bundled panels (Lucide, Emoji, Palettes, Google Fonts curated list)
# work offline and need no env vars.

# Unsplash — search photos. Free dev tier: 50 req/hour.
# Sign up: https://unsplash.com/developers (create an app, copy "Access Key")
UNSPLASH_ACCESS_KEY=

# Pexels — search photos and videos. Free, 200 req/hour. (Tier 2)
# Sign up: https://www.pexels.com/api/
PEXELS_API_KEY=

# Pixabay — search photos / illustrations / vectors. Free, 100 req/60s,
# instant key (email signup, no review). CC0-equivalent license.
# Sign up: https://pixabay.com/api/docs/
PIXABAY_API_KEY=

# Google Fonts — full catalog API. Optional in Tier 1 (we ship a hand-curated
# allowlist of ~100 fonts as static JSON), only needed if you later want to
# enable the "show all" toggle that browses the full Google Fonts catalog.
# Sign up: https://developers.google.com/fonts/docs/developer_api
GOOGLE_FONTS_API_KEY=

# Tensorix — OpenAI-compatible AI gateway (EU-hosted). Powers the AI Edit
# feature (element + section mode). See plan at
# `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-17-ai-edit-element-section.md`.
# Without these, the AI Edit tool renders a "not configured" state.
# Sign up: https://app.tensorix.ai
TENSORIX_API_KEY=
TENSORIX_BASE_URL=https://api.tensorix.ai/v1
TENSORIX_DEFAULT_MODEL=minimax/minimax-m2
TENSORIX_FALLBACK_MODEL=z-ai/glm-5.1
